<section class="px-6 lg:px-12 py-[100px] max-w-[960px] mx-auto text-center">
  <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-[var(--accent)] font-semibold mb-3.5">The backstory</div>
  <h2 class="text-[32px] lg:text-[40px] font-bold tracking-[-1.5px] mb-14 leading-[1.15] text-[var(--text)]">Why Tomoro exists.</h2>

  <div class="max-w-[680px] mx-auto relative text-left">
    <div class="absolute -top-10 -left-6 text-[160px] leading-none text-[var(--accent)] opacity-[0.06] pointer-events-none select-none" style="font-family: Georgia, serif;" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</div>
    <div class="text-lg lg:text-xl text-[var(--text)] leading-[1.75] relative z-10 space-y-5">
      <p>I'm a freelancer. For years I bounced between spreadsheets, Toggl, Harvest — tools that either did too little or charged too much for features I'd never use.</p>
      <p>I wanted something simple: a place to organize my projects, log what I worked on, and know what to bill. No cloud accounts. No $10/month subscriptions. Just a quiet app on my desktop that works.</p>
      <p>So I built it. Tomoro is the tool I wished existed.</p>
